title: "feat(snowbridge): simulate Ethereum export blobs on Bridge Hub using XCM executor"
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Bridge Hub now performs an execution-aligned dry-run for Snowbridge v2 Ethereum export blobs
    before enqueueing an outbound message. The export wrapper runs the inner blob under a dedicated
    XCM executor configuration with a simulation-only transactor and weight trader, exercising the
    same barrier, aliasing policy, and structural checks as real XCM execution while keeping the
    simulation side-effect free.

    Invalid or malformed contract-call parameters are rejected consistently and result in a Bridge
    Hub asset trap (via `AssetTrap = PolkadotXcm`) rather than silently failing after a successful
    simulation. Structural validation for the v2 outbound shape is centralized and reused by both
    the converter and the simulation barrier.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    When an Ethereum-bound XCM export contains an invalid beneficiary shape or an invalid/malformed
    contract call, Bridge Hub will now trap the involved assets instead of attempting to enqueue an
    outbound message.
crates:
- name: snowbridge-outbound-queue-primitives
  bump: minor
- name: bridge-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: bridge-hub-westend-integration-tests
  bump: none
